; ToustovacVirtualMic.inf - Toustovač Clean Microphone (WaveRT, capture only).;; Root-enumerated endpoint. Product-owned GUIDs (generated once, committed; in native/virtual_mic/README.md):;   control interface : {A3F5D6B1-2C8E-4A7F-9B1D-6E2F0C8A4417};   endpoint (mic)    : {B72E94C4-1D3F-5A86-BC0A-9D7421E3F2B0};; Hardware ID: ROOT\VIVERRA\TOUSTOVAC_CLEAN_MIC. The endpoint name is the; friendly name below; abbreviated UI alias kept by the same GUID pair so Edge; device selection stays stable across restart and in-place upgrade.[Version]Signature   = "$WINDOWS NT$"Class       = MEDIAClassGuid   = {4d36e96c-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}Provider    = %Viverra%CatalogFile = ToustovacVirtualMic.catDriverVer   = 09/19/2026,1.0.0.0PnPLockdown = 1[Manufacturer]%Viverra% = Viverra, NTamd64[Viverra.NTamd64]%Toustovac.Clean.Mic.Name% = ToustovacVirtualMic, ROOT\VIVERRA\TOUSTOVAC_CLEAN_MIC[ToustovacVirtualMic]Include   = machine.infNeeds     = PCI_NOT_STARTED_ON[ToustovacVirtualMic.Interfaces]; KS audio categories keep the standard GUIDs.  The private control; interface (broker-only, SDDL-restricted inside the driver) is registered; by the driver itself (IoRegisterDeviceInterface), not from this INF.AddInterface = %KSCATEGORY_AUDIO%, "TOP", InterfaceTOPAddInterface = %KSCATEGORY_CAPTURE%, "TOP", InterfaceTOP[InterfaceTOP]AddReg = InterfaceAddReg[InterfaceAddReg]; Standard, documented media-category registration only; the IPolicyConfig; default-mic is left untouched on purpose.HKR,,%KSCATEGORY_AUDIO%,,TOP[Strings]Viverra                  = "Viverra"Toustovac.Clean.Mic.Name = "Toustovač Clean Microphone"KSCATEGORY_AUDIO         = "{6994AD00-93EF-11D0-A3CC-00A0C9223196}"KSCATEGORY_CAPTURE       = "{65E8773D-8F56-11D0-A3B9-00A0C9223196}"